    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered list of everything that fires when you `POST /api/owners`, traced through `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:126`).\n\n## Validations (in the order they fire)\n\n**0. Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` (line 124). Requires `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`. Only enforced when `petclinic.security.enable=true`. Denial \u2192 403.\n\n**1. Bean Validation on the DTO** \u2014 `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, fires before the method body. On `OwnerFieldsDto`:\n- `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words, `' -` separators)\n- `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`)\n- `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n- `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n- `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n- `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)` (optional)\n- `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")` (optional)\n\nFailure \u2192 400.\n\n**2. `normalizeAddress`** (line 127) \u2014 *mutation*: trim, collapse whitespace, uppercase, expand ST/RD/AVE. (Runs before the remaining checks so they see the canonical value.)\n\n**3. `validateRequiredFields`** (line 128) \u2014 rejects blank/whitespace-only firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone \u2192 400.\n\n**4. `validatePostcode`** (line 129) \u2014 if postcode present and city maps to a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD), postcode must fall in that region's range \u2192 400 otherwise.\n\n**5. `normalizeTelephone`** (line 130) \u2014 *mutation + validation*: convert to E.164 (assumes `+61` for leading `0`; enforces digit-count rules per country code); invalid \u2192 400.\n\n**6. `normalizeEmail`** (line 131) \u2014 *mutation + validation*: trim, must match email pattern, lowercase, reject disposable domains (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail) \u2192 400.\n\n**7. `rejectDuplicateIdentity`** (line 132) \u2014 scans all owners; exact match on `telephone|email|householdId` \u2192 409.\n\n**8. `rejectDuplicateHousehold`** (line 133) \u2014 skipped if `sharesHousehold=true`; else any existing owner with the same `householdId` (SHA-256 of lastName+postcode) \u2192 409.\n\n**9. `rejectCityAtCapacity`** (line 134) \u2014 \u2265 50 existing owners in that city (case-insensitive) \u2192 409.\n\n**10. `rejectFutureRegistrationDate`** (line 135) \u2014 supplied `registrationDate` after today \u2192 400 (checked on the raw value, before defaulting).\n\n**11. `defaultRegistrationDate`** (line 136) \u2014 *mutation*: default null \u2192 today, then roll Sat\u2192Mon / Sun\u2192Mon to a business day.\n\n**12. `rejectDailyLimit`** (line 137) \u2014 \u2265 100 existing owners on the business-day-adjusted date \u2192 **429**.\n\n## Side-effects (after validation passes)\n\n**13. Map DTO \u2192 entity** (line 139, `OwnerMapper.toOwner`) \u2014 ignores `id` and `pets`; `sharesHousehold` is not persisted. The entity already carries the normalized address, E.164 telephone, lowercased email, and defaulted registrationDate from the mutations above.\n\nThen these derived fields are computed and set on the entity (most scan all existing owners):\n- **14. `assignCustomerCode`** (line 140) \u2014 `<REGION>-<HASH8>` from region + SHA-256(telephone+lastName).\n- **15. `assignHouseholdId`** (line 141) \u2014 12-hex SHA-256 of lastName+postcode.\n- **16. `assignHouseholdMemberCount`** (line 142) \u2014 count of same-household owners + 1.\n- **17. `assignNamesakeCount`** (line 143) \u2014 count of pre-existing owners with same first+last name.\n- **18. `assignMembershipNumber`** (line 144) \u2014 `<customerCode>-M<YY>`.\n- **19. `assignBulkSignupWarning`** (line 145) \u2014 `true` if > 80 existing owners share the registrationDate.\n- **20. `assignPossibleDuplicate`** (line 146) \u2014 flags `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` when a same-lastName+postcode owner exists with a different phone (unless declared household member).\n\n**21. Persist** (line 147, `clinicService.saveOwner` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save`) \u2014 single `@Transactional` INSERT into `owners`; id via `GenerationType.IDENTITY`. No related entities created.\n\n**22. Audit log** (lines 148\u2013149) \u2014 `AUDIT.info(\"owner created id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026 membershipLevel=\u2026\")` to the dedicated `AUDIT` SLF4J logger, only after a successful save.\n\n**23. Build response** (lines 150\u2013153) \u2014 map to `OwnerDto` (adds read-only derived fields: displayName, initials, membershipLevel/points, locality, etc.), set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, return **201 Created**.\n\nNotable negatives: **no** `@PrePersist`/JPA lifecycle callbacks, **no** custom `ConstraintValidator` on this path, and **no** events, emails/notifications, or cache updates.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: nearly every business check and derived field (steps 7\u20139, 12, 14, 16, 17, 19, 20) calls `findAllOwners()` and scans the full table in memory \u2014 so a single owner creation triggers many full-table loads and won't scale."
